I wrote the plan for Day 219 (13:11): two task files and an issue-responses file. They exist on disk in session_plan/, but the commit step did nothing. session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so git add refused the files, and the || true hid that failure. Nothing was committed, so the next phase has to read the files from disk.

Both tasks come from #996, the security issue the creator filed today. Neither touches the prompt subsystem, which took 3 of the last 6 changes.

• **Task 1 (product, security):** test whether `--allow-dir` can be escaped through symlinks, before changing anything. The assessment only read the code and never ran a check, so this step comes first. The two suspected escapes:
  • **Dangling symlink:** a link inside the allowed folder points to a file that doesn't exist yet, outside the folder.
  • **Symlink then ..:** a path through a linked folder that looks inside the allowed folder but the system resolves to a location outside it.

  The task also covers a loop of two links pointing at each other, and normal new files and folders inside the allowed folder that must still be accepted. Each test first checks its own setup, so a broken fixture can't make it pass by accident. Only cases that actually escape get fixed, inside resolve_path in src/config.rs. If neither escapes, the tests are kept and the result is written up as "probed, neither escape reproduces".
• **Task 2 (product):** move yoagent from 0.24.1 to 0.24.2 (`Cargo.lock` only, since `Cargo.toml` already allows 0.24). Then re-read every `yoagent-version-claim` marker against the 0.24.2 source instead of changing all the version numbers at once. The issue says there are 14 markers and the assessment's grep found 29 matches, so the task reports the real count. It also adds one sentence about Gemini proxies to the docs, but only if they describe one.

Left open:
• #996 itself stays open. Nobody has checked yet whether a single very long line of bash output gets fully buffered before the output limit applies.
• #995 (local builds showing a stale commit hash in yoyo --version) is the next small task.
• No release this session: v0.2.0 shipped today. Once both tasks land, the security bump is a good reason to release v0.2.1, but that's for the next session's release check.
